;; The read-back that makes the answer query answerable. Where a value is,
;; in the verb of its kind: a person lives in the house it shares, owns
;; what it owns, drinks what it drinks, smokes what it smokes, and is
;; a member of the house it shares.
(top  smoker-and-house instance Smoker House)
(top  drinker-and-house instance Drinker House)
(top  owner-and-house instance Owner House)
(top  color-and-house instance Color House)
(top  thing-and-house instance Thing House)
(meet same-house smoker-and-house smokes)
(meet same-house drinker-and-house drinks)
(meet same-house owner-and-house owns)
(meet same-house color-and-house lives-in)
(meet same-house thing-and-house has)

;; A verb and its passive are converses, and a verb of a person goes through
;; the house the person lives in: a person smokes what is smoked in their
;; house, drinks what is drunk in their house, owns what they own, and lives
;; in the house they share.
(converse smokes smoker-and-house)
(converse drinks drinker-and-house)
(converse owns owner-and-house)
(converse lives-in smoker-and-house)

;; The hypothesis mechanism: the obligations of the theory step 2 selected.
;; The program states no other mechanism.
(solve :no-search)
